"""The connections of the users to the APIs with the authorization code flow (ADR 0033).

A user connects an account of a third-party service, and the app calls
the API of the service with the access token of the user. `POST
/auth/connections/<api>` gives the URL of the page where the signed-in
user allows the access. The authorization server sends the browser back
to `GET /auth/connections/<api>/callback` with a code. The app changes
the code for the tokens of the user (with PKCE), and keeps them in the
table `api_connections`, encrypted with a key from `AUTH_SECRET`.

A client of the API reads the access token of the user (`UserToken`), and
gets a new access token with the refresh token a little before the token
ends, or after an answer with the status 401.

The signed `state` of the flow holds the user, a nonce, and the page to go
back to (`return_to`, a page of a front end in `CORS_ORIGINS`). The PKCE
verifier is an HMAC of the nonce, so no URL has it. With `return_to`, the
callback sends the browser back to the page with `#connected=<api>` or
`#error=...` in the fragment of the URL. Without `return_to`, the callback
returns the connection as JSON.
"""

